config KDLOCK_REBUILD
	bool "kdlock private mutex core for source rebuild"
	depends on X86_64 && !PREEMPT_RT
	select EXECMEM
	help
	  Package the source-rebuilt ordinary mutex core, task-owned storage,
	  immutable-text provider, executable image loader and bounded compiler
	  control channel. The exact Linux 7.0 task fields and lifecycle hooks
	  must already be integrated. Resource counts and complete auxiliary
	  control-stack bounds are explicit provider inputs, without defaults.

	  All admitted source dependencies must remain immutable through their
	  actual native, generated and feedback users. This option supplies no
	  automatic Linux mutex selection. Generic rwsem bindings remain explicit;
	  unselected objects keep native behavior. Enabling this option alone
	  establishes no build, execution or performance evidence.
	  See kernel/integration/BUILDING.md in the kdlock package.

config KDLOCK_RW_WAIT_DIAG
	bool "Temporary ordinary rwsem worker wait counters"
	depends on KDLOCK_REBUILD
	default n
	help
	  Add explicit per-task opt-in aggregate counters for the ordinary rwsem
	  diagnostic. The provider owns preallocated rows through complete drain.
	  No event logging, scheduler activation claim or lock policy change.
	  Disabled versus enabled overhead must be measured on the same image.

config KDLOCK_RWSEM_NODE_WAIT
	bool "Ordinary rwsem writers wait for their MCS turn separately"
	depends on KDLOCK_REBUILD
	default n
	help
	  Keep ordinary task-owned uninterruptible native writers off the shared
	  rwsem wait queue until they own their MCS turn and need reader drain or
	  WAKE completion. The predecessor's existing direct task wake supplies
	  turn progress. Selected writers register and recheck before sleeping.
	  Callable, killable and managed writer paths keep their existing waits.
	  This candidate is independent of KDLOCK_RW_WAIT_DIAG and has no measured
	  performance or live-kernel correctness result.
